Headless engine mode: the host application owns the audio focus.

Kodi requests the audio focus whenever playback starts or resumes, and abandons it on pause and
stop. A host application running Kodi as its playback engine (KODI_ENGINE_MODE) requests the
focus itself and pauses Kodi when it loses it; Kodi's own requests would take the focus away
from the host and make it pause playback.

